  "scope": "Atomic large sparse edit and undo/redo with verified notification content; domain only, no rendered-frame or desktop performance budget claim.",
  "method": "Two fresh Node --expose-gc processes per background. Full 6400x6400 four-layer background (empty or golden-verified heartland). Two edit layers each seed 200 rows x 100 four-cell runs. Replace with eight-cell runs crossing storage/visual boundaries, clipped only in fixture construction at x=6400. Timing includes command generation/copies, storage, inverse capture, compaction, history accounting and validating notification listener. Post-GC heapUsed + arrayBuffers deltas include runtime/JIT and changed storage/history, not physical app footprint. External already includes ArrayBuffers. Before/after memory snapshots do not establish transient heap peak; maxRSS is the whole process high-water mark. A tiny edit under maxEntries=1 evicts the large history entry for a release measurement; GC outside timing. Full edited-layer equality and background hashing outside operation timing. No percentile claim from two samples.",
